<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">speed</ansi>

<ansi fg="cyan">Speed</ansi> measures how quickly you move and react. A faster fighter lands more
blows and is harder to pin down.

<ansi fg="yellow">Combat</ansi>

* Sets your chance to hit. At equal Speed you hit {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.ToHitEven" }}% of the time. Each
  point you are faster moves that 1/{{ config "GamePlay.Combat.StatEdgeSpan" }} of the way to {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.ToHitMax" }}%, and each point
  slower 1/{{ config "GamePlay.Combat.StatEdgeSpan" }} of the way down to {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.ToHitMin" }}%. Stats grow slowly, so one
  point matters (<ansi fg="command">help stat-edge</ansi>).
* Increases your chance to parry a melee blow with your weapon, against the
  attacker's speed (<ansi fg="command">help defense</ansi>).
* Each point of Speed over a foe's Perception makes your tackles likelier
  (<ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>).
* Speed and your own burden set your action tempo for every weapon type,
  with at most {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.MaxTurnsPerRound" }} turns per combat round (<ansi fg="command">help tempo</ansi>).
* Increases the number of your unarmed damage dice when fighting without a weapon.

<ansi fg="yellow">Movement</ansi>

* Reduces the action-point cost of moving between rooms, letting you travel
  more quickly each round.
</ansi>
